# Customer Prompt: Example Customer Name
#
# HOW TO USE:
#   1. Copy this file to v3/knowledge/customers/<slug>.md
#   2. The slug is the customer's lookup key (email or name), lowercased,
#      with non-alphanumeric characters replaced by underscores.
#      Examples:
#        "Bavarian Bier Cafe"        → bavarian_bier_cafe.md
#        "info@bavarianbier.com.au"  → info_bavarianbier_com_au.md
#   3. Fill in only the sections relevant to this customer.
#      Delete sections that don't apply — empty sections add noise.
#   4. This file is gitignored (may contain customer-specific details).
#      The .example version is tracked as a template.
#
# WHEN TO CREATE ONE:
#   - This customer's PO format confuses the general rules
#   - Their column headers are unusual or ambiguous
#   - They use a non-standard SKU labelling convention
#   - Their documents include their own internal product codes that look like ours

## Document Format Notes

Describe the layout of this customer's typical Purchase Order or document:

- Their POs are generated from [ERP system name, e.g. MYOB / SAP / Xero]
- Supplier code appears in the column labeled "[exact column header]"
- Customer's own item code appears in "[exact column header]"
- Quantity is in "[exact column header]", UOM in "[exact column header]"
- Their delivery date field is labeled "[exact label]"

## SKU / Product Code Rules

Notes about which column holds our supplier code vs their internal reference:

- Column "Supplier Code" / "Vendor Code" = our product code (put in `sku`)
- Column "Our Ref" / "Stock Code" = their internal code (put in `customer_ref`)
- Their codes always start with [prefix, e.g. "BBC-"] — if you see that prefix, it is their code

## Customer Identification Notes

Notes to help identify this customer's name/entity correctly on their documents:

- The company name appears as "[exact text on document]" in the [From/Buyer/etc] field
- Their ABN is [ABN] — use this to confirm identity if name is ambiguous
- Their billing email is [email]

## Known Edge Cases

Any recurring extraction problems and how to handle them:

- Page 2 is always a Terms & Conditions page — ignore it for line items
- They sometimes include a "freight line" at the bottom — exclude it (description contains "Freight" or "Delivery")
- Their document header repeats on each page — only extract line items, not the header rows
